I implemented the node's real function, but I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `https://metadata.internal.example/...` would need filesystem and HTTP authority the node doesn't have. Sending the input's text to an external service would also go beyond the node's declared authority. If operations needs either one, the graph's `with` clause has to grant it, for example `http-client` for the fetch.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let q = query.query;
        let knowledge = crate::aap::caps::kb_read::lookup(&q.question);
        ConversationContext {
            intent: q.intent,
            question: q.question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

